1
00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:06,921
Cooperation under Pressure Our cooperative project began with vigour Everyone wanted to

2
00:00:06,934 --> 00:00:12,618
move forward but nobody could foresee every obstacle When supplies ran short

3
00:00:12,803 --> 00:00:16,908
the leader refused to make a rash promise We had to wrestle

4
00:00:16,921 --> 00:00:21,921
with the schedule and choose tactics that protected quality One member wanted

5
00:00:21,934 --> 00:00:27,934
to head straight into production Another preferred to wait indefinitely We chose

6
00:00:27,947 --> 00:00:32,934
a middle course preserve stability and test a small batch A follower

7
00:00:32,947 --> 00:00:38,790
could contribute judgment rather than simply repeat instructions The experience was unique

8
00:00:38,803 --> 00:00:43,882
in its details but familiar in its lesson Even an enthusiastic group

9
00:00:43,895 --> 00:00:48,658
can fall behind when responsibilities remain unclear We should not leave a

10
00:00:48,671 --> 00:00:52,789
gap in planning and hope goodwill will fill the void Nor should

11
00:00:52,803 --> 00:00:57,921
a slack schedule encourage careless work We must reckon with uncertainty and

12
00:00:57,934 --> 00:01:00,605
turn common intentions into specific action
